      "title": "Instructions for using the University’s recruitment system",
      "description": "Instructions for using the University’s recruitment system | University of Helsinki Skip to main content Home Home Close Support us University of Helsinki News News News and press releases War in Ukraine Think Corner Events calendar Public examinations Unitube videos Press and media services Newsletters University on social media Close menu Admissions and education Admissions and education Search for programmes and courses Apply to bachelor's and master's programmes Apply to doctoral programmes For international students Open university Apply for exchange and visiting studies Continuous learning Education Apply to supplementary studies Admission Services and Study Guidance Close menu Research Research Explore our research, our research units, services for researchers and our top-notch research infrastructures. Top research areas and researchers Find a researcher Research units and infrastructures Doctoral school Research integrity Services for researchers Close menu Innovations and cooperation Innovations and cooperation Innovations, services and collaboration opportunities for researchers, businesses, alumni and donors. For decision-makers Innovations and entrepreneurship Support us For alumni Business collaboration and partnership International cooperation Close menu About us About us Strategy, economy and quality This is the University of Helsinki Sustainability and responsibility Careers People Archive and registration services Processing of data at the University Book a venue Visit us Close menu Faculties and units Faculties and units Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Theology Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Swedish School of Social Science Close menu Support us Home About us Careers at the University of Helsinki Open positions Instructions for using the University’s recruitment system Instructions for using the University’s recruitment system On this page you will find instructions on how to use the recruitment system. In the need of support, you will receive assistance from: recruitment@helsinki.fi. Find out more – Frequently asked questions Important information regarding the choice of email address when registering Due to a technical issue, email addresses managed by Elisa (@kolumbus.fi, @elisanet.fi, @saunalahti.fi) currently cannot be used to register in the University of Helsinki's SAP SuccessFactors recruitment system. The issue is being investigated, and we apologize for any inconvenience this may cause. We kindly ask applicants to use an alternative email address not managed by Elisa (such as Gmail, Outlook, etc.) when registering and applying for open positions. Thank you for your understanding! Close I am a new job applicant New users can register here: https://jobs.helsinki.fi/ Opens in a new tab You can also access the above web address by clicking on Apply for the position in a job ad published at https://www2.helsinki.fi/en/open-positions . When registering, we first ask for your email address, to which the system will send a verification code. We recommend using an email address other than one ending in @helsinki.fi during registration. Enter the verification code sent to your email on the registration page. Using a verification code during registration enhances the secure handling of applicants' contact information. After that, we will ask for a password, your name, and your country/region of residence. Before creating a username, you must read and accept the privacy statement. The system will direct you to your applicant profile. You will also receive a message confirming your registration to the email address you provided. System functions: Profile: Here you can submit an application for an open position and explore your applicant profile and application history. You can also change the system language and reset your password in the settings. When applying for an open position, remember to attach all required documents to your application. Please note that the attachments are always connected to a specific application and that a curriculum vitae is always required. If applying for several positions in our system, the attachments you added most recently will appear in your profile as attachments connected to your previous applications, too. However, such attachments are not actually connected to your previous applications. My documents: Here you can see your most recently saved curriculum vitae (CV). Profile information: Here you can see the name and email address you saved during registration. You can also add your phone number and country of residence here and edit these profile details if necessary. Search options and privacy: Here you can read the University of Helsinki’s privacy statement. If you reject it by selecting Revoke, your account will be permanently deleted. Jobs applied: Here you can see all positions for which you have applied. If necessary, you can edit an application you have submitted if it has not yet progressed to the assessment stage. You can also cancel an application. Please note that if you cancel an application, you can restore it once and then apply again for the same open position using the same profile. Saved applications: Here you can continue to complete applications saved as drafts. View all jobs: Here you can find the University of Helsinki’s open positions. Select the position you are interested in and apply. View by category: Here you can browse the University of Helsinki’s open positions based on various categories. Careers: This will take you to the University of Helsinki’s career website. Close Logging in to the recruitment system You can log in to the system here: https://jobs.helsinki.fi/ Opens in a new tab If you are currently employed by the University, please see the section I am a University employee applying for a new position . If you forget your password, you can request a link to reset it by clicking on Forgot your password?. If an account in the system corresponds to the information you enter, you will receive instructions by email to reset your password. Close I am a University employee applying for a new position If you are currently employed by the University of Helsinki, you can apply for open positions here: https://msap.sap.helsinki.fi/flp Opens in a new tab Select Employee login Log in with your University username (‘AD account’) and password. You can also find a direct link to the system in the Tools section on Flamma: Recruitment system. If you apply for an open position through a job ad on the University website, the system will recognise you as a University employee based on your @helsinki.fi email address, and you will receive an error message concerning your username. If you do not wish to apply for a position as a current employee, you must register a new username using an email address other than your @helsinki.fi address. Further information on registration can be found under I am a new job applicant . Close I tried to log in to the system with a University email address, but received an error message. Why? Our system recognises you if you are currently employed by the University or have previously worked at the University. This may result in an error message indicating that your @helsinki.fi email address is already in use. If you work for the University, please see the section I am a University employee applying for a new position . If you do not currently work for the University, you should register a new username using an email address other than your @helsinki.fi address (see I am a new job applicant ). Close I have not received a confirmation message regarding my registration. Why? Occasionally, a short-lived fault in the system may lead, for example, to a confirmation message not getting sent. Please contact recruitment@helsinki and we will investigate the situation to enable you to move on. Close I have not received a confirmation message regarding the submission of an application. Why? Please first double-check that you have submitted the application. In your applicant profile, you can view your applications on the Jobs applied tab and your incomplete applications on the Saved applications tab. If you cannot find the application you are looking for on either of these tabs, please search for the position in the View all jobs menu and submit an application. Close Can I change the language of the system? You can select the language of the system when logging in by opening the language menu. The system can be used in Finnish, Swedish and English. Please check your browser’s language settings if you cannot access the recruitment system in the language of your choice. Close How can I ensure that the information I entered has been saved? The recruitment system automatically saves all information you enter, but please remember to click on Save at the bottom of the page if you leave the page in question or do not wish to submit your application yet. Close Can I continue to complete my application later or cancel my application? Yes. You can save your application at any time before submitting it. Incomplete applications that you have saved can be found on the Saved applications tab. You can also cancel an application. You can find the positions for which you have applied on the Jobs applied tab. Please note that if you cancel an application, you can restore it once and then apply again for the same open position using the same profile. Close Can I supplement or edit my application after sending it? You can access your applicant profile to edit and supplement your application information and attachments if the application process has not yet progressed to the assessment stage. If applying for several positions in our system, the attachments you added most recently will appear in your profile as attachments connected to previous applications. However, such attachments are not actually connected to your previous applications. Close Can I submit an open application? If you are interested in the University as an employer, but no suitable position is currently available, we recommend you contact the unit that interests you and ask about job opportunities. Close Attachments You can check the attachments connected to your application in the system by accessing your profile and clicking on Jobs applied -> My documents. If applying for several positions in our system, the attachments most recently added will appear in your profile as attachments connected to your previous applications, too. However, such attachments are not actually connected to your previous applications. Close At what time do application processes end? Application processes ends on the date indicated in the job ad at 23.59 local Helsinki time (EEST). Close Supported browsers and file formats We recommend that you use Mozilla Firefox or Google Chrome as your browser. Cookies and pop-ups must be enabled in your browser settings. Application attachments must be in PDF or DOCX format. The maximum size of each attachment is 5 MB. Close Why is my login denied (error GBC451)? Users from embargoed countries Users are not permitted to use SAP SuccessFactors services from embargoed countries. Therefore, a user that travels to an embargoed country is prohibited from using our services while in that embargoed country. Users can access SAP SuccessFactor services after returning to a non-embargoed country. For the list of such countries/regions, please go through: https://www.sap.com/about/agreements/export-statements.html Opens in a new tab Note: When users are blocked it starts a clock of 24hrs, the user should only retry to login after those 24hrs and when outside the embargoed country. Close Data Protection, University of Helsinki recruitment system At the University of Helsinki, we value your privacy and your right to protect your personal data. Everyone has the right to know what data concerning them are being kept and how those data are processed. On this website, we collect data protection statements pertaining to the processing of personal data at the University of Helsinki: Data protection | University of Helsinki Close Back Open positions Summer jobs Employment programme for people with disabilities Trainee programme for international masters students Instructions for our recruitment system Instructions for the applicants of teaching and research positions This is how we recruit The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service Up Campuses The University operates on four campuses in Helsinki and in ten other locations. See all City Centre Campus Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Law Faculty of Theology Faculty of Social Sciences Swedish School of Social Sciences Kumpula Campus Faculty of Science Viikki Campus Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Meilahti Campus Faculty of Medicine University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3\n(Fabianinkatu 33)\n00014 University of Helsinki\nSwitchboard:\n+358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Quick links Library Careers and open positions Webshop Contact information People finder Contact details and building opening hours Invoicing details Press and Media Give feedback For the university community Studies service for current students Flamma-intranet Cookie management About the website Accessibility statement Data protection © University of Helsinki 2026"
    },
    "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/about-us/careers/open-positions/instructions-applicants-teaching-and-research-positions": {
      "title": "Instructions for applicants of teaching and research positions",
      "description": "Instructions for applicants of teaching and research positions | University of Helsinki Skip to main content Home Home Close Support us University of Helsinki News News News and press releases War in Ukraine Think Corner Events calendar Public examinations Unitube videos Press and media services Newsletters University on social media Close menu Admissions and education Admissions and education Search for programmes and courses Apply to bachelor's and master's programmes Apply to doctoral programmes For international students Open university Apply for exchange and visiting studies Continuous learning Education Apply to supplementary studies Admission Services and Study Guidance Close menu Research Research Explore our research, our research units, services for researchers and our top-notch research infrastructures. Top research areas and researchers Find a researcher Research units and infrastructures Doctoral school Research integrity Services for researchers Close menu Innovations and cooperation Innovations and cooperation Innovations, services and collaboration opportunities for researchers, businesses, alumni and donors. For decision-makers Innovations and entrepreneurship Support us For alumni Business collaboration and partnership International cooperation Close menu About us About us Strategy, economy and quality This is the University of Helsinki Sustainability and responsibility Careers People Archive and registration services Processing of data at the University Book a venue Visit us Close menu Faculties and units Faculties and units Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Theology Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Swedish School of Social Science Close menu Support us Home About us Careers at the University of Helsinki Open positions Instructions for applicants of teaching and research positions Instructions for applicants of teaching and research positions On this page, you can find instructions for applicants for teaching and research positions. In academic recruitment the principles and recommendations of the responsible researcher evaluation are followed. More detailed instructions on how to apply for a single position can be found in the job advertisement or on the Faculty's website. Academic portfolio The academic portfolio can be used to assess academic competence. The portfolio is a way to record and document one's core competence and to cover aspects of academic work (research, teaching, societal interaction and administration) as a whole. The aim is to create an organised documentation of one’s professional skills and strengths and to give a concise portrayal of one’s professional growth. An ex­ample of the struc­ture of an aca­demic port­fo­lio 1. Ba­sic infor­mation First names and family name (also previous family names) Education and degrees Other necessary background information (no private personal details needed, relevant contact information is given in application form) 2. Research and sci­entific activ­it­ies Experience in research and other scientific activities Research philosophy and ethics, primary fields of research Significant publications Research assessments and awards Activities in the academic community Visions and personal development plans Other scientific merits. 3. Teach­ing and su­per­vi­sion Experience in undergraduate and postgraduate teaching and supervision Pedagogical approach and training Published study materials and use of educational technology Development of teaching and awards for teaching Participation in the assessment and development of teaching Strengths, development challenges and visions of one's teaching Other teaching-related qualifications. 4. Ad­min­is­tra­tion and other activ­it­ies Administrative and management duties Duties in one's field outside the University Active role in society and positions of trust Publications, presentations and dissemination of scientific knowledge through other means Other significant merits and duties. The recommended length for an academic portfolio is 4-7 pages plus the enclosures. Individual faculties and units may have the specific guidelines and recommendations of their own regarding the structure, extent and requisite enclosures. When applying for a teaching or research post at the university, one should always make sure whether the faculty or unit has given their own instructions on how to create one’s academic portfolio. The portfolio is also a tool for enhancing one’s competence and development. Close Language proficiency requirements The person performing the university's teaching and research position is required to master the language in which he or she must provide teaching. In universities where a degree can be completed in both Finnish and Swedish, the person performing the teaching and research position is also required to have at least satisfactory oral and written skills in Finnish and Swedish. The University may grant exemption from these language proficiency requirements as laid down in the Regulations of the University of Helsinki. Swedish These requirements cover all Swedish-language positions. When the language of instruction is Swedish, the language proficiency recommended for successfully attending to the duties of the position corresponds with level C2 of the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages. At the faculty’s discretion, level C1 of the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages may be accepted as a minimum Swedish language proficiency requirement. During the recruitment process, language proficiency is demonstrated with documents, an interview and a teaching demonstration. If needed, applicants may be requested to provide further clarification of their language proficiency. In Swedish-language positions, language proficiency can be verified in the following ways A Civil Service Language Proficiency Certificate, a National Certificate of Language Proficiency or Swedish language proficiency demonstrated through studies can be used as part of demonstrating Swedish language proficiency in the following manner: Civil Service Language Proficiency Certificate: excellent oral and written skills (C 2), good oral and written skills (C 1) National Certificate of Language Proficiency: skill level 6 (C 2), skill level 5 (C 1) Studies: Education completed in Swedish and a maturity test completed at a higher education institution in Swedish/a matriculation examination with at least magna cum laude approbatur in Swedish as a native language/a matriculation examination with at least eximia cum laude approbatur in Swedish as a second language (C 2) Education completed in Swedish/a maturity test completed at a higher education institution in Swedish/a matriculation examination with a passing grade in Swedish as a native language/a matriculation examination with at least magna cum laude approbatur in Swedish as a second language (C 1) Instead of or alongside a certificate, Swedish language proficiency can also be demonstrated in other ways. In assessing applicants, language proficiency will be taken into account both when assessing applicants’ qualifications for appointment to the position in question and their mutual ranking. English In practice, teaching and research tasks require good English language skills. Close Assessment of teaching skills The assessment of teaching skills plays a key role in the overall assessment of applicants in recruitment processes. Applicants’ teaching skills are assessed if they apply for a teaching or research position or for the title of docent. Each faculty has a committee for the assessment of teaching skills, set up by the dean. The Teaching demonstration The teaching skills committee conducts a reasoned overall assessment of applicants’ teaching skills. A demonstration of teaching skills is a public teaching session in the field of the position or docentship applied for, and plays a key role in the overall assessment of teaching skills. The areas to be assessed in addition to the teaching demonstration are defined in the relevant matrix for the assessment of teaching skills. The purpose of a teaching demonstration is to verify the applicant’s teaching skills in practice. The teaching demonstration must be seen as a learning situation and in the teaching demonstration, the applicant teaches as in a genuine teaching situation. The teaching demonstration is not a scientific presentation.  When assessing the teaching demonstration, priority will be paid to how the applicant is able to guide and promote the learning of participants. Close Template for researcher's curriculum vitae A curriculum vitae (CV) is an overview of an individual’s studies, professional career, academic merits and other achievements. The aim of the template is to provide guidelines for the writer of a CV so that the individual’s merits are presented as comprehensively, truthfully and comparably as possible. The University of Helsinki recommends applicants use the cv model created by The Finnish National Board on Research Integrity (TENK). There is no need to include personal details irrelevant for academic merits, like for example date of birth or home address. More information about the template for researcher's curriculum vitae Opens in a new tab Close National classification for publications The Ministry of Education and Culture has drawn up a classification of publication types. It can be utilised or its use may be required in the recruitment of the University of Helsinki. National classification for publications Opens in a new tab Close Recruitment process Read more User instructions for recruitment system Read more Academic positions and titles Read more Back Open positions Summer jobs Employment programme for people with disabilities Trainee programme for international masters students Instructions for our recruitment system Instructions for the applicants of teaching and research positions This is how we recruit The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service Up Campuses The University operates on four campuses in Helsinki and in ten other locations. See all City Centre Campus Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Law Faculty of Theology Faculty of Social Sciences Swedish School of Social Sciences Kumpula Campus Faculty of Science Viikki Campus Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Meilahti Campus Faculty of Medicine University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3\n(Fabianinkatu 33)\n00014 University of Helsinki\nSwitchboard:\n+358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Quick links Library Careers and open positions Webshop Contact information People finder Contact details and building opening hours Invoicing details Press and Media Give feedback For the university community Studies service for current students Flamma-intranet Cookie management About the website Accessibility statement Data protection © University of Helsinki 2026"
    },
    "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/about-us/careers/open-positions/how-we-recruit": {
      "title": "An open recruitment process that values every candidate",
      "description": "An open recruitment process that values every candidate | University of Helsinki Skip to main content Home Home Close Support us University of Helsinki News News News and press releases War in Ukraine Think Corner Events calendar Public examinations Unitube videos Press and media services Newsletters University on social media Close menu Admissions and education Admissions and education Search for programmes and courses Apply to bachelor's and master's programmes Apply to doctoral programmes For international students Open university Apply for exchange and visiting studies Continuous learning Education Apply to supplementary studies Admission Services and Study Guidance Close menu Research Research Explore our research, our research units, services for researchers and our top-notch research infrastructures. Top research areas and researchers Find a researcher Research units and infrastructures Doctoral school Research integrity Services for researchers Close menu Innovations and cooperation Innovations and cooperation Innovations, services and collaboration opportunities for researchers, businesses, alumni and donors. For decision-makers Innovations and entrepreneurship Support us For alumni Business collaboration and partnership International cooperation Close menu About us About us Strategy, economy and quality This is the University of Helsinki Sustainability and responsibility Careers People Archive and registration services Processing of data at the University Book a venue Visit us Close menu Faculties and units Faculties and units Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Theology Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Swedish School of Social Science Close menu Support us Home About us Careers at the University of Helsinki Open positions An open recruitment process that values every candidate An open recruitment process that values every candidate Every applicant matters to us. We want our recruitment process to be open, fair and respectful at every stage. Learn more about how we recruit and the principles that guide our recruitment. Recruitment at the University of Helsinki Timely applicant communication We are committed to open and timely communication throughout the recruitment process. Applicants are informed clearly and at the right stages about the progress of the process. Our goal is to create a positive and trustworthy applicant experience, where every candidate feels valued and respected. Openness and transparency Openness and equal opportunities are core values guiding our recruitment. Open positions are clearly described in job ads, including the selection criteria  and are open to both current University of Helsinki employees and external applicants. Many of our positions are also open to international candidates, supporting the University’s goal of attracting diverse talent and strengthening our international community. Professional selection process Our selection process is based on clearly defined criteria and high-quality evaluation. We apply diverse methods and the expertise of several specialists to ensure that all selections are made objectively and on a well-founded basis. Each recruitment supports the University of Helsinki’s strategic objectives, the quality of research and teaching, and our shared values. We also apply sanctions imposed by the European Union in our recruitment processes, which means that we check the applicant’s situation with regard to the sanctions, and we do not offer an employment relationship or other agreement to persons under EU sanctions. The University is committed to Open, Transparent and Merit-based Recruitment of Researchers (OTM-R), as defined by the European Commission. This approach ensures that we use the most appropriate methods to find the most suitable candidates, safeguarding equality, fairness and respect throughout the process, and enhancing the attractiveness of research careers. Recruitment stages The recruitment process can vary depending on the position. The process associated with tenure track positions is described here. Equality and public nature of recruitment The University of Helsinki is an equal and non-discriminatory employer, which also guides our recruitment. As we value a diverse work community, we wish to recruit to the University experts with different backgrounds. Recruitment decisions are made on the basis of the information obtained from the applicant or during the recruitment process. Decisions are based on predetermined assessment criteria. We pay attention to the quality of recruitment. In the recruitment of teaching and research personnel and in the assessment of career progression, we follow the recommendations and principles of responsible evaluation of a researcher. The University of Helsinki is an organisation under public law, making our recruitment partially public. Recruitment decisions as well as the applicants and their applications, are public. Documents containing evaluation of applicants are confidential and will not be disclosed to anyone other than the parties involved. In information requests, all private personal information is redacted, and the work associated with this will be invoiced according to the university's general practices . The university does not publish information about applicants without a specific request or reason. For feedback about recruitment, please contact the recruiting supervisor directly or HR at recruitment@helsinki.fi . Come work with us – for the world! Explore the positions currently open and apply now! Read more Discover our work culture Read more Read more on career options at UH Read more Back Open positions Summer jobs Employment programme for people with disabilities Trainee programme for international masters students Instructions for our recruitment system Instructions for the applicants of teaching and research positions This is how we recruit The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service Up Campuses The University operates on four campuses in Helsinki and in ten other locations. See all City Centre Campus Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Law Faculty of Theology Faculty of Social Sciences Swedish School of Social Sciences Kumpula Campus Faculty of Science Viikki Campus Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Meilahti Campus Faculty of Medicine University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3\n(Fabianinkatu 33)\n00014 University of Helsinki\nSwitchboard:\n+358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Quick links Library Careers and open positions Webshop Contact information People finder Contact details and building opening hours Invoicing details Press and Media Give feedback For the university community Studies service for current students Flamma-intranet Cookie management About the website Accessibility statement Data protection © University of Helsinki 2026"
    },
    "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/about-us/careers/open-positions/accessibility-statement-our-recruitment-service": {
      "title": "The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service",
      "description": "The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service | University of Helsinki Skip to main content Home Home Close Support us University of Helsinki News News News and press releases War in Ukraine Think Corner Events calendar Public examinations Unitube videos Press and media services Newsletters University on social media Close menu Admissions and education Admissions and education Search for programmes and courses Apply to bachelor's and master's programmes Apply to doctoral programmes For international students Open university Apply for exchange and visiting studies Continuous learning Education Apply to supplementary studies Admission Services and Study Guidance Close menu Research Research Explore our research, our research units, services for researchers and our top-notch research infrastructures. Top research areas and researchers Find a researcher Research units and infrastructures Doctoral school Research integrity Services for researchers Close menu Innovations and cooperation Innovations and cooperation Innovations, services and collaboration opportunities for researchers, businesses, alumni and donors. For decision-makers Innovations and entrepreneurship Support us For alumni Business collaboration and partnership International cooperation Close menu About us About us Strategy, economy and quality This is the University of Helsinki Sustainability and responsibility Careers People Archive and registration services Processing of data at the University Book a venue Visit us Close menu Faculties and units Faculties and units Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Theology Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Swedish School of Social Science Close menu Support us Home About us Careers at the University of Helsinki Open positions The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service The Accessibility Statement of University of Helsinki recruitment service. The online services provided by University of Helsinki are to follow the accessibility requirements in the Act on the Provision of Digital Services. The purpose of this accessibility statement is to inform about the accessibility of our services and how to give feedback on the accessibility. Read more about accessibility at University of Helsinki. This accessibility statement deals with the service www.jobs.helsinki.fi Opens in a new tab . The statement has been devised 1.11.2023, and updated 8.1.2025. The Act on the Provision of Digital Services applies to the service. The act states that all public online services must be accessible. This statement is based on an accessibility report made by an external accessibility expert on November 1st, 2023. Status of the digital service’s accessibility The requirements are met partly. Non-accessible content The website does not yet meet the requirements fully. The detected shortcomings are divided according to the contents of the accessibility report. Visuals The text contrast in the file upload element is not satisfactory when a file is uploaded into it and the the cursor is hovering over it. (WCAG 1.4.3) Structure The confirmation page after sending a job application does not have a programmatic heading. (WCAG 1.3.1) The search field’s current label is not descriptive. (WCAG 1.3.1, 2.4.6) The main navigation includes objects that utilize the aria-haspopup property, contrary to the ARIA specification. (WCAG 4.1.2) Not every page has a unique and descriptive title. (WCAG 2.4.2) The service includes content, such as language links and some job vacancy pages, that differs from the user interface’s language and does not have its own language defined. (WCAG 3.1.2) The service’s language menu has been implemented in several different ways in different pages of the service and it has been named differently in each one. (WCAG 4.1.2, 3.2.4) The file upload elements have a complicated program and naming structure. The programmatic structure also differs from its visual implementation. (WCAG 1.3.1) There are invisible text elements (“emphasized”) in the modal dialog, which screen readers interpret as being programmatically connected to certain buttons. These buttons are not visually emphasized, which leads to screen readers getting the wrong view of them. (WCAG 1.3.1) There is an unnamed button element among the language buttons on the email notifications’ control page. (WCAG 4.1.2) Navigation The breadcrumb trail is not implemented in a programmatically consistent way on the different pages of the service. This is especially confusing for screen reader users. (WCAG 1.3.1) It is not possible to get to the front page from all pages of the service. (WCAG 2.4.5) Several navigation landmark elements have been used in the service’s footer, but they have not been labeled. Hence, they are not distinguishable from one another. (WCAG 4.1.2) The service’s skip link has been implemented in a way that does not allow for keyboard use in the Safari browser. (WCAG 2.1.1) The location of elements in the service’s header changes depending on what page you are currently on, and whether or not you are logged in. Some elements move from the header area to the main content area on certain pages. (WCAG 3.2.3) Form elements The fields asking for the user’s information are not marked programmatically correctly for utilizing autocomplete, which would aid the user in filling in the correct information. (WCAG 1.3.5) Conflicting information regarding filling in fields is provided when attempting to change the password using a screen reader. Messages are not programmatically connected to their fields. (WCAG 1.3.1) The service’s combobox elements do not work reliably with the most common screen reader and browser combinations, nor do they fully follow the ARIA specification (WCAG 4.1.2). The elements are labeled with non-descriptive content. (WCAG 2.4.6) The instructions for the Telephone number field on the job application page do not work reliably using some of the most common screen reader and browser combinations (WCAG 1.3.1). The notifications do not work reliably about having reached the maximum amount of characters in the free text field of the job application on some of the most common screen reader and browser combinations. Also, the message does not remain visible, making it indetectable as text on the page (WCAG 1.3.1). Parsing The service has some errors when it comes to labeling start and end tags, as well as the elements being nested according to their specifications. (WCAG 4.1.1) Evaluation method External evaluation: an external actor who has not taken part in the planning and development of the site has made the accessibility evaluation. Did you notice an accessibility shortcoming in our digital service? You can give feedback on accessibility via email at rekrytointi@helsinki.fi . Title your message (Accessibility feedback) and write in your message which page and what kind of problem your feedback concerns. Replying can take as long as 14 days. University of Helsinki Recruitment Services is responsible for the accessibility and feedback handling of the jobs.helsinki.fi-website. Supervisory authority If you notice accessibility issues on the site, please give feedback to us, the administrator of the website, first. Replying can take as long as 14 days. If you are not satisfied with the reply or do not receive a reply within two weeks, you may file a complaint with the Finnish Transport and Communications Agency Traficom Digital Accessibility Supervision Unit Opens in a new tab . Traficom’s accessibility requirements website (saavutettavuusvaatimukset.fi) has detailed instructions on how to file a complaint and how the issue will be handled. Contact information of the supervisory authority Finnish Transport and Communications Agency Traficom Digital Accessibility Supervision Unit www.webaccessibility.fi Opens in a new tab saavutettavuus@traficom.fi telephone switchboard 029 534 5000 Back Open positions Summer jobs Employment programme for people with disabilities Trainee programme for international masters students Instructions for our recruitment system Instructions for the applicants of teaching and research positions This is how we recruit The Accessibility Statement of our recruitment service Up Campuses The University operates on four campuses in Helsinki and in ten other locations. See all City Centre Campus Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Law Faculty of Theology Faculty of Social Sciences Swedish School of Social Sciences Kumpula Campus Faculty of Science Viikki Campus Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Meilahti Campus Faculty of Medicine University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3\n(Fabianinkatu 33)\n00014 University of Helsinki\nSwitchboard:\n+358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Quick links Library Careers and open positions Webshop Contact information People finder Contact details and building opening hours Invoicing details Press and Media Give feedback For the university community Studies service for current students Flamma-intranet Cookie management About the website Accessibility statement Data protection © University of Helsinki 2026"
    },
    "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/about-us/university-helsinki/contact-details": {
      "title": "Contact details of the university",
      "description": "Contact details of the university | University of Helsinki Skip to main content Home Home Close Support us University of Helsinki News News News and press releases War in Ukraine Think Corner Events calendar Public examinations Unitube videos Press and media services Newsletters University on social media Close menu Admissions and education Admissions and education Search for programmes and courses Apply to bachelor's and master's programmes Apply to doctoral programmes For international students Open university Apply for exchange and visiting studies Continuous learning Education Apply to supplementary studies Admission Services and Study Guidance Close menu Research Research Explore our research, our research units, services for researchers and our top-notch research infrastructures. Top research areas and researchers Find a researcher Research units and infrastructures Doctoral school Research integrity Services for researchers Close menu Innovations and cooperation Innovations and cooperation Innovations, services and collaboration opportunities for researchers, businesses, alumni and donors. For decision-makers Innovations and entrepreneurship Support us For alumni Business collaboration and partnership International cooperation Close menu About us About us Strategy, economy and quality This is the University of Helsinki Sustainability and responsibility Careers People Archive and registration services Processing of data at the University Book a venue Visit us Close menu Faculties and units Faculties and units Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Theology Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Swedish School of Social Science Close menu Support us Home About us We are the University of Helsinki Contact details of the university Contact details of the university The contact information of the University of Helsinki. Address and switchboard University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3 (Fabianinkatu 33) 00014 University of Helsinki Building opening hours Switchboard: +358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Admission and student services Admissions and study advice to all University of Helsinki applicants and students is offered by HelsinkiUni Help Opens in a new tab . In our online service you can: Search for content with an AI boosted search feature Chat with experts every weekday from 9:00 to 15:00. Please choose “Applying to University of Helsinki” when you start the chat so the conversation is forwarded to the right expert. Submit a service request. Service requests are answered on weekdays. Please note that during rush hours, our experts might have several ongoing chat conversations simultaneously. If you need more in-depth advice, the best option is often to submit a service request directly. Contact HelsinkiUni Help Read more Archives and Registry Postal address: Archives and Registry, PO Box 3, 00014 University of Helsinki registry@helsinki.fi Phone numbers : +3582941 22222 (Registry), +3582941 22390 (Archives) Archive and registration services Read more Faculties Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 27 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Latokartanonkaari 7, Helsinki Close Faculty of Arts Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 24 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Metsätalo: Unioninkatu 40, Helsinki Porthania: Yliopistonkatu 3, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Biological and Environ­mental Sciences Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 65 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Viikinkaari 1, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Edu­ca­tional Sciences Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 9 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Siltavuorenpenger 5, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Law Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 64 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Siltavuorenpenger 1, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Medicine Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 63 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Biomedicum Helsinki 1: Haartmaninkatu 8 Biomedicum Helsinki 2: Tukholmankatu 8 Close Faculty of Pharmacy Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 56 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Viikinkaari 5 E, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Science Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 64 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Physicum: Gustaf Hällströmin katu 2, Helsinki Exactum: Pietari Kalmin katu 5, Helsinki Chemicum: A.I. Virtasen aukio 1, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of So­cial Sciences Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 54 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Unioninkatu 37, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Theo­logy Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 3 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Fabianinkatu 33, Helsinki Close Fac­ulty of Veter­in­ary Medicine Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 66 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Agnes Sjöbergin katu 2, Helsinki Close The Swedish School of So­cial Science Postal ad­dress P.O. Box 16 00014 University of Helsinki Visiting address Yliopistonkatu 3, Helsinki Snellmaninkatu 12, Helsinki Close Looking for these? People finder Read more Press and media Read more Management Read more Opening hours Read more Campuses Read more Invoicing details Read more Back Contact details Opening hours University of Helsinki invoicing details Up Campuses The University operates on four campuses in Helsinki and in ten other locations. See all City Centre Campus Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Educational Sciences Faculty of Law Faculty of Theology Faculty of Social Sciences Swedish School of Social Sciences Kumpula Campus Faculty of Science Viikki Campus Faculty of Agriculture and Forestry Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences Faculty of Pharmacy Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Meilahti Campus Faculty of Medicine University of Helsinki P.O. Box 3\n(Fabianinkatu 33)\n00014 University of Helsinki\nSwitchboard:\n+358 (0) 2941 911 (mobile call charge / local network charge) Quick links Library Careers and open positions Webshop Contact information People finder Contact details and building opening hours Invoicing details Press and Media Give feedback For the university community Studies service for current students Flamma-intranet Cookie management About the website Accessibility statement Data protection © University of Helsinki 2026"
